spec_validator._check_confidence_range (WI-nurun) checks an edge's
confidence against the derived band of its evidence_type. The merge
pass's corroboration (ADR-0057 s13) sets confidence to the declared
corroboration level (0.95 by default, configurable under [merge]) and
keeps the incumbent's evidence_type, so every edge two producers agreed
on read as out of band. ir.py defines confidence_source=corroborated as
"not either producer's value": the band does not apply.

Measured on the first scip-python-enabled self-map (after WI-nijod):
109,622 cross_field|info notes, every one confidence_source=corroborated
(ast_call_direct 67,471, ast_call 35,227, ast_name_read 6,924), and
check-self-tree-validation exit 1 (109622 > baseline 0). The fixed check
over the same map's 352,232 edges: 0.

